points.explanation:
{でしょう} adds **probability**: 'probably', 'I think', 'I expect'. You'll hear it every day in weather forecasts:

{明日[あした]は雨[あめ]でしょう。} 'It will probably rain tomorrow.'

It attaches to plain forms:

- Nouns and {な}-adjectives directly: {雨[あめ]でしょう}, {静[しず]かでしょう}
- {い}-adjectives: {寒[さむ]いでしょう}
- Verbs in plain form: {来[く]るでしょう}, {来[こ]ないでしょう}

It often comes with {たぶん} (maybe, probably).

With a rising tone, {でしょう？} checks that the listener agrees: 'right?'. In casual speech, {でしょう} becomes {だろう} (when guessing) or {でしょ？} (when checking).
